      "exceptions": ["Specific language, removal of all imperative code, monadic/category-theory vocabulary and replacing every exception with a custom algebraic type are not required."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 490,
          "quote": "The vocabulary is optional; the law is not.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRealisation%20shape",
          "start_line": 490
        }
      ],
      "key": "profile_realisation_shape",
      "statement": "Semantic steps should read as transforms over admitted truth; effects should be explicit and at the edge. Needing orchestration code, workspace state, service methods or fallback defaults to discover meaning indicates excessive imperative coupling. Implementation must remain readable, modular and honest about meaning/effects. Where higher-order or effectful computation is composed, an explicit composition/effect algebra is required with applicable identity, closure, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws. The core should remains a recommendation; the algebra requirement remains mandatory.",
      "uncertainty": "The profile's adoption rule and full composition law are not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["requirement_classification", "requirements_surface", "successor_disposition"],
      "conditions": ["For every live requirement family and every inherited or legacy requirement."],
      "exceptions": ["Paths, filenames or packaging may belong in requirements when themselves constitutional."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 526,
          "quote": "A live requirement\nis incomplete if either axis is missing. In project documents the\nclassification is explicit in the requirement's header metadata: `Status`\ncarries lifecycle status and `Category` carries the kind.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification",
          "start_line": 523
        }
      ],
      "key": "requirement_classification_rules",
      "statement": "Classify every live family by both Status and Category in header metadata; neither may be missing and nothing live remains unclassified. All categories remain constitutional, not priority/user-facing labels; requirements need not become marketed features and should avoid premature mechanisms. Deferred retains an explicitly not-yet-operative/realised obligation with honest deferment, never current closure. Superseded transfers ownership and requires Implements and Supersedes on the governing design record. Active needs a written/updated owning design decision. Orphaned is removed or explicitly superseded. These statuses/categories/legacy classes, evidence classes, migration old-path/inherited/implementation classes, ADR statuses and change classes are declared states, never core results. Active/material advance is not satisfied; Deferred/Orphaned is not falsified. Evaluations produce their own predicate-bound core values. Successor work separately assigns RELEASE dispositions: Active can be semantically superseded, Superseded does not establish an accepted successor relation, and Orphaned is not authorised intentional removal.",
      "uncertainty": "Details of classifications defined in unsupplied migration, ADR and change sections remain external."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["requirements_surface", "design_surface", "realisation", "constitutional_chain"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": ["A live requirement can remain unrealised with explicit honest deferment."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 582,
          "quote": "Ownership: every live requirement family maps to one or more owning design\ndecisions; every ADR or other design record grounds itself in requirements\nthrough an explicit `Implements:` line",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FTrace%20closure%20and%20anti-drift",
          "start_line": 580
        }
      ],
      "key": "constitutional_trace_closure",
      "statement": "Every live requirement family has one or more design owners; every design record has explicit Implements grounding. Every live requirement is realised through design/code/tests or honestly deferred. Shipping code/tests trace to live requirement and design authority; hidden ungoverned Product behaviour is prohibited even if functional. Unowned requirements, ungrounded design, undocumented deferment and ownerless behaviour are drift. Tests of implementation habit lock in drift. Persistent event/projection delta triggers intake diagnosis among code, requirement/design stack, predictive model and observation. Capability without scenario has unverified operational meaning. Feature-labelling guarantees/governance/verification misclassifies them; in-place constitutional correction corrupts history. An unexpressible real-use gap re-enters Requirements or upstream at its change-class layer, not through a code hack.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["constitutional_chain", "realisation", "design_surface"],
      "conditions": ["For artifacts already published as live constitutional surfaces."],
      "exceptions": ["Implementation surfaces remain refactorable while mutable.", "Retained superseded responsibility must satisfy the referenced migration retention relation."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 631,
          "quote": "Live domain artifacts, once published as live\nconstitutional surfaces, are immutable in place; if one is wrong, the valid\nactions are to supersede it with a new version or to withdraw or delete it\nfrom the live surface.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FLive%20surface%20immutability",
          "start_line": 621
        }
      ],
      "key": "constitutional_history_immutability",
      "statement": "Multiple live surfaces may accumulate as versioned constitutional history, never scratch space. Incorrect live artifacts are superseded, withdrawn or deleted from the live surface, not silently mutated. Superseded transitional paths/scaffolds/fallbacks retire and have no permanent authority; retained responsibility satisfies the migration closure relation. Preserve past through version control, operational event history where present and superseded artifacts. Compatibility shims need not ship forever.",
      "uncertainty": "The referenced §7 retention relation is not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["operational_lifecycle", "product_definition_surface", "requirements_surface", "design_surface"],
      "conditions": ["Where lifecycle posture materially affects Product meaning or an invariant obligation."],
      "exceptions": ["Not-applicable phases require reasons.", "Deferred phases require named deferment and a later-resolution owner surface."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 667,
          "quote": "Silent absence is not a valid lifecycle answer.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FOperational%20lifecycle%20sufficiency",
          "start_line": 661
        }
      ],
      "key": "lifecycle_sufficiency_and_gap_states",
      "statement": "Product Definition and requirements supply enough constitutional signal for downstream lifecycle derivation or explicitly record ambiguity, without specifying every mechanism. Product names boundary, use, release/install, live-use, observability and retirement/supersession posture; requirements state governing lifecycle/ownership/source-truth/authority/interpretation obligations. Every phase is answered, inapplicable with reason, or a named Gap:/Unanswered:. This is ambiguity detection, not a requirement that each requirement become a release plan. Missing signal cannot be supplied by local convention, implementation precedent, prompt prose or fixtures: reprice the constitutional owner or carry explicit governed debt. Phase states map to no core value; answered/inapplicable cannot substitute for satisfied, and evaluations return independent predicate-bound results.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["outcome_work_wave"],
      "conditions": ["For every product-outcome-bearing work wave."],
      "exceptions": ["An assurance capability explicitly defined as Product behaviour may count as product progress; its evidence still does not author the claim."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 708,
          "quote": "Acceptance exhausts only that instance and its\ndeclared acceptance interval; it does not discharge an enduring guarantee,\na recurring obligation or a broader product family beyond the accepted\ninstance.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation",
          "start_line": 702
        }
      ],
      "key": "outcome_progress_and_acceptance_scope",
      "statement": "Judge progress and supported-path promotion against the same selected outcome and acceptance interval. Only accepted material advance projects progress; bounded prerequisite work names the enabled obligation, preservation/repeated proof is useful but not progress, and regression adds no progress. Owner acceptance ends that instance's selection of further progress work; witnesses remain preservation/regression evidence. Further work is preservation, another admitted outcome's named bounded prerequisite, or a new lawfully repriced change, never extra progress on the accepted instance. Selecting another existing unresolved outcome is goals/sequencing; changing meaning/scope or introducing an outcome re-enters Product. Evidence-surface completion cannot select/enlarge/replace outcomes. An artifact's Product-output and evidence roles must be separately declared.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["outcome_work_wave", "realisation"],
      "conditions": ["For material realisation growth within a product-outcome-bearing wave."],
      "exceptions": ["Admission or renewal may be performed by an explicitly bounded proxy of the owning work-wave authority."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 751,
          "quote": "Ended authority cannot be renewed by repair,\ncontinuation, evidence, active ticket or run state, or prior admission;\nfurther material work requires a new admission by the owning authority or\nits explicitly bounded proxy",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation",
          "start_line": 748
        }
      ],
      "key": "growth_admission_and_exhaustion",
      "statement": "Growth requires the selected unresolved outcome, an admitted named bounded prerequisite, or an admitted named bounded experiment whose stated observation discriminates a stated decision for that outcome. A prerequisite/experiment grants only its provisional bound, not enlarged outcome, downstream work, promotion, closure or waived design/safety/authority/release law, including applicable design-profile prime law. Record owner/proxy admission in durable goals/ticket authority with bound and exhaustion/falsification condition. A decision-discriminating observation exhausts its experiment. Ticket/contract drafting or validation, active status and prior admission cannot create/extend/renew authority. Outcome acceptance, prerequisite discharge, experiment decision resolution, any admitted terminal condition, rejection, withdrawal, supersession, repricing-away or evidence falsification ends the basis. Further material work needs new admission.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["outcome_work_wave", "realisation"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": ["Independent parallel work may proceed under its own admitted basis.", "Affected-path promotion may resume after repair, repricing or owner acceptance."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 765,
          "quote": "A regression or unresolved gap blocks further promotion on the affected\npath until repaired, repriced or accepted by the owning authority.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation",
          "start_line": 760
        }
      ],
      "key": "retention_and_path_limited_promotion",
      "statement": "Retention as supported behaviour, evidence, regression protection or bounded donor material grants no growth authority. Consumers own deletion/archive/quarantine/salvage mechanics; salvage carries only explicitly re-adopted semantics, not enclosing authority, dependencies, completion or work-selection power. Regression or unresolved gap blocks only its affected promotion path until repaired, repriced or owner-accepted; independent admitted work is not globally serialised and cannot be counted as this outcome's progress. Outcome success is necessary delivery evidence, not complete Product/release closure.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["constitutional_chain", "spec_method"],
      "conditions": ["For every substantive change."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 771,
          "quote": "Every substantive change begins with intake triage, an explicit declared\nchange intent and a lawful re-entry point into the constitutional chain",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management",
          "start_line": 769
        }
